    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "2 Bedroom End-of-Terrace Residence | Approx. 64.64 sq. m. | BER D | Side Access | Rear Garden\n\nLiam Reilly Auctioneers are delighted to present No. 83A Courtown Park, Kilcock, Co. Kildare to the market.\n\nThis well-proportioned two-bedroom end-of-terrace residence extends to approximately 64.64 sq. m. (696 sq. ft.) and enjoys an attractive position within this established residential development, immediately adjoining a large open green area.\n\nThe property offers bright and practical accommodation arranged over two floors and is presented in good condition throughout. The ground floor comprises an entrance hall, comfortable living room with feature fireplace, and a generously sized kitchen/dining room with fitted units and direct access to the rear.\n\nUpstairs, there are two well-proportioned double bedrooms, together with a family bathroom fitted with bath, electric shower, wash-hand basin and WC.\n\nExternally, the property benefits from a lawned front garden, while the end-of-terrace position provides valuable pedestrian side access leading to the rear. The rear garden is mainly laid in lawn and incorporates a paved area and useful block-built storage shed. The garden offers excellent potential for a purchaser wishing to further enhance the outdoor space.\n\nThe property has a BER rating of D.\n\nWith its manageable size, two double bedrooms and convenient location, No. 83A Courtown Park should appeal to a broad range of purchasers, including first-time buyers, downsizers and investors.\n\nAccommodation\nEntrance Hall\nBright entrance hallway with tiled flooring, radiator and staircase to first-floor accommodation.\n\nLiving Room 3.9m x 3.0m\nBright front-facing reception room overlooking the green, with timber-effect flooring and feature fireplace with marble-style surround and hearth.\n\nKitchen / Dining Room 3.9m x 3.8m\nGenerous kitchen/dining area with tiled flooring and a good range of fitted wall and floor units, countertop work surfaces, tiled splashback, stainless-steel sink, electric hob, oven and extractor hood. Plumbed for washing machine. Window and door provide natural light and access to the rear garden. Useful understairs storage.\n\nBedroom 1 4.0m x 3.0m\nSpacious double bedroom with timber-effect flooring, radiator and large window providing excellent natural light.\n\nBedroom 2 3.9m x 2.9m\nAnother generous double bedroom with timber-effect flooring, radiator and window overlooking the surrounding area.\n\nBathroom 2.1m x 2.1m\nFitted with bath and electric shower, pedestal wash-hand basin and WC. Tiled floor and tiled bath/shower surround. Frosted window providing natural light and ventilation.\n\nOutside\nLawned front garden with the property enjoying an attractive outlook adjoining a substantial open green area. Gated pedestrian side access leads to a private rear garden, mainly laid in lawn with mature planting and a useful block-built storage shed.\n\nFeatures\n•Two-bedroom end-of-terrace residence \n•Approx. 64.64 sq. m. / 696 sq. ft. \n•BER D \n•Two well-proportioned double bedrooms \n•Generous kitchen/dining room \n•Separate living room with feature fireplace \n•Large open green immediately adjoining the property \n•Gated side access \n•Private rear garden \n•Block-built garden shed \n•Established residential development \n•Convenient to Kilcock town centre \n•Excellent road and rail connections \n•Ideal first-time buyer, downsizer or investment property \n\nLocation\nCourtown Park is conveniently situated close to the centre of Kilcock, a thriving and increasingly popular commuter town offering an excellent range of everyday amenities including shops, supermarkets, cafés, restaurants, schools, sporting clubs and recreational facilities.\n\nKilcock also benefits from excellent transport connectivity. Kilcock railway station provides rail services towards Dublin, while the town is included within TFI's Dublin Commuter Zone 2. Road access is particularly convenient via the nearby M4 motorway, providing direct connectivity towards Maynooth, Leixlip and Dublin as well as westwards towards the Midlands.\n\nThe town's public transport connectivity is also set to improve significantly: in March 2026, Transport for Ireland confirmed plans to extend DART services to Kilcock, including an upgraded station and infrastructure designed to support substantially increased service frequency when the project becomes operational. \n\nWith Maynooth also within easy reach, Kilcock is particularly well positioned for purchasers seeking a more relaxed residential setting while retaining convenient access to Dublin and the wider commuter belt.\n\nViewing is highly recommended and strictly by appointment with Liam Reilly Auctioneers.\n\nLIAM REILLY AUCTIONEERS give notice that; All descriptions, dimensions, references to condition and necessary permissions for the use and occupation, and other details are given in good faith and are believed to be correct, but any intending purchasers should not rely on them as statements or representations of fact but must satisfy themselves by inspection or otherwise as to the correctness of each of them.\n\n"
      },
